  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "The concentration of the ions for drinking water are,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.2</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>ppm</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.05</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>ppm</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.0</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>ppm</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.0</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>ppm</mi></math><br /><br />Here, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> concentration is greater than the allowed limit.&nbsp;So, it makes the water sample unsuitable for drinking."
  }
